  'outsourced-assistant-approval-queue': `An approval queue should help the named owner answer a bounded question, not pressure that person through volume. Put the requested action, evidence cutoff, affected record, and consequence of waiting in a predictable order. An outsourced assistant can remove duplicate packets, check that the source is present, and flag a stale item. A Filipino assistant may prepare a comparison between the submitted version and the proposed change, but should not turn a familiar pattern into approval. When an owner responds with a condition, preserve the condition beside the decision and tell the next assistant exactly which actions remain permitted. Review returned items separately from rejected items. Keep the route-local article dated 2026-08-21 so its approval boundary remains explicit and route-specific.`,
  'filipino-assistant-data-cleanup-scope': `A Filipino assistant should treat an exception ledger as a valid outcome of cleanup, not as evidence that the routine failed. For each untouched record, preserve the identifier, field, source consulted, rule considered, reason for stopping, and question for the owner. This lets the owner improve the approved scope without asking the assistant to guess. Separate normalization from merge, deletion, and overwrite because their consequences differ. After a sample is approved, record the exact rule version and the date checked. If an edge case repeats, compare it with the original examples before changing the rule. The route-specific record dated 2026-08-21 should show that careful data preparation can be useful to an outsourced assistant while final authority over protected or ambiguous data remains with the owner.`,
  'outsourced-assistant-research-brief': `A research brief becomes reviewable when every important sentence has a visible evidence status. Label it supported, narrower inference, unresolved, or unsuitable, and name the population and period that label refers to. An outsourced assistant can read primary material, compare definitions, and flag a mismatch for a Filipino research assistant or owner to inspect. The assistant should not turn a headline, search snippet, or vendor claim into a factual conclusion. Preserve inaccessible sources and explain how that limitation affects the proposed wording. Before use, ask whether the conclusion would change if the missing evidence contradicted it. Keep methodology, evidence analysis, limitations, and conclusion in this route-local record dated 2026-08-21. That discipline supports a useful brief without inventing credentials, results, or certainty.`,
  'outsourced-assistant-meeting-prep-packet': `A good meeting packet separates preparation from participation. The outsourced assistant can assemble approved evidence, verify links, show the requested decision, and identify the unanswered question. The owner and participants decide priorities, commitments, and sensitive interpretation. For a distributed team, include a zone beside each relevant time and identify the preparation cutoff in calendar terms. A Filipino assistant can maintain a decision index that records whether each item is confirmed, conditional, deferred, or open. After the meeting, preserve the packet version used and link each answer to an approved note or explicit owner decision. If an item had no accountable decision owner, keep it open rather than implying that discussion resolved it. This route-local packet is bound to 2026-08-21 and keeps meeting preparation useful without claiming an outcome.`,
  'outsourced-assistant-vendor-follow-up': `A follow-up record should make the next safe attempt obvious while protecting the underlying obligation. Record the original request, known contact path, latest verified reply, checkpoint, time zone, and stop condition. An outsourced assistant can ask the same approved question and log the response. A Filipino assistant can prepare a comparison when a supplier proposes a substitute, but the owner must decide whether the proposal changes terms or commitments. Do not label silence as agreement, and do not label an estimate as a promise. If a message arrives through an unexpected channel, verify it before sharing information. Review the queue for stale checkpoints and preserve the original wording beside any new proposal. The route-local record dated 2026-08-21 keeps vendor follow-up bounded and traceable.`,
