  'filipino-virtual-assistant-calendar-timezone-rules': `A time-zone rule should be checked against a concrete invitation, not only described abstractly. Record the canonical zone, confirmed participant zones, calendar date, local displays, duration, daylight-saving status, and the person who approved an exception. A Filipino virtual assistant can prepare options and show the conversion, while the owner decides whether protected time or a customer commitment may move. If someone says tomorrow, write the actual date and ask for confirmation. If an event crosses midnight, show both dates. If the zone is inferred rather than confirmed, stop and label the uncertainty. After booking, inspect the invitation and source message together. This route-local guidance is explicitly dated 2026-08-21 and keeps calendar preparation auditable for an outsourced assistant team.`
